WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
- Like maybe we'll make
this work, but now...

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.433
Oh, God.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.410
I recently discovered
this old YouTube challenge

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.830
where people tried to bake cookies

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.740
blindfolded and without a recipe.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.080
So I thought it'd be fun to challenge

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.353
my coworkers here at
BuzzFeed to do the same.

00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:19.063
♪ One, two, three, four ♪

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:20.880
- Yeah, I could probably bake a cookie

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.056
without a recipe.

00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:24.380
- [Cameraman] What about
doing it while blindfolded?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.213
- Oh, oh.

00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:26.046
- No!

00:00:26.046 --> 00:00:27.430
No, I can't do that!

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.320
- I think I could definitely
bake cookies blindfolded.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.470
- I mean, red's my color.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.050
It matches my lipstick
so we're already off

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.470
to a great start.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.640
- All right, everyone, let's watch me

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.670
make cookies blindfolded with no recipe.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.810
God help me.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.660
- Okay, I'm currently trying to figure out

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.960
where all my ingredients are.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:44.920
I've got chocolate.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.780
Wait, I have to check.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.230
- Probably start by putting
all the dry ingredients

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.500
together, and then slowly
adding the wet ingredients.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.760
- I'm gonna start with the hardest part

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.060
which I think is the eggs.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.580
- Oh, that is not sugar.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.120
(laughing) I don't know what this is.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.590
- [Emily] This feels like
it's not a half a cup.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.080
- All measuring has gone out the window

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.070
since I can't even see it anyway.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:05.903
- [Emily] You're supposed to crack an egg

00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:07.826
on the table not the bowl.

00:01:07.826 --> 00:01:09.100
It's supposed to not
leave shells that way.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.790
- Gotta be careful with vanilla.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.623
How do I do this?

00:01:11.623 --> 00:01:12.710
Maybe I just...

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.560
- My confidence level is plummeting.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.950
- We've got two sizes: big and small

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.430
so maybe you're the salt.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:23.076
Ew, definitely the salt.

00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:25.760
- [Noga] I need one teaspoon of this

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.180
so I hope that's enough.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.030
- This is feeling kind
of like cookie dough.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.200
- More chocolate.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.750
Can you have too much chocolate?

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.711
No.

00:01:34.711 --> 00:01:35.544
No.

00:01:35.544 --> 00:01:37.990
- [Kuwilileni] I can already
tell the texture is really off.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.830
- [Noga] This feels pretty good.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:40.860
- No turning back now.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.440
We're in the final stages
of these delicious cookies

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.640
you guys can make at home

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.430
if you've been following along.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.040
- So I think these will cook like cookies,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.313
but I don't think they're
gonna look like cookies.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.740
- Cool.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.513
- I'm just now looking down.

00:01:57.513 --> 00:02:00.950
It looks like a baby threw up on a tray.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:01.783
- You know what?

00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:03.160
I'm curious to see what's gonna happen

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.660
so let's put them in the oven.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.490
- They look okay.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.580
Have I seen better cookies?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.603
Absolutely.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.583
- Whoo.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.300
Oh, no.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.720
You know it's not horrible.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.573
They didn't quite rise to the occasion.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.960
- [Kuwilileni] So I thought
they were gonna look

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.110
a lot better than they actually do.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.410
They look really biscuity.

00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:31.040
- I mean, I think these are dope.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.890
There even gooey too.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.630
All right, let's give it a try.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.870
- You only live once.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.720
Let's...

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.660
It tastes like bread with
chocolate chips in it.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.240
On a scale of one to ten,

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.620
the cookies I made today are a five.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.760
- I rate this cookie sheet ten out of ten.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.626
I didn't know I needed one whole cookie,

00:02:53.626 --> 00:02:56.320
but sometimes you just
get what you deserve.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.450
- I think like everything went wrong.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.940
Like, I think it tastes okay.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:00.773
Like, it tastes good.

00:03:00.773 --> 00:03:01.970
I think the chocolate makes it good,

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.920
but like the texture's not at all right.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.980
- I'm really proud of this actually.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.610
Yeah, they're like crispy on the ends.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.250
This is great.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.370
Hell, yeah.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.466
- It probably doesn't look good,

00:03:13.466 --> 00:03:14.503
but I like it.

00:03:16.274 --> 00:03:18.857
(upbeat music)

